WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
How can you map a living human brain without opening the skull?

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.200
Magnetic resonance imaging, or MRI, pictures brain structure.

3
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.800
Functional MRI adds glowing patches during a task.

4
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.660
What do those glowing patches measure?

5
00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:24.063
Structural MRI maps gray matter, white matter and lesions.

6
00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:30.123
Functional MRI reads blood instead, through hemoglobin's magnetism.

7
00:00:31.423 --> 00:00:36.643
Oxygen-poor hemoglobin, deoxyhemoglobin, disturbs the scanner's magnetic field;

8
00:00:37.423 --> 00:00:39.403
oxygen-rich hemoglobin barely does.

9
00:00:40.723 --> 00:00:45.203
Active regions receive more oxygenated blood than they use, so that disturbance

10
00:00:45.203 --> 00:00:51.563
shrinks. Seconds later, the blood-oxygen-level-dependent, or BOLD, signal rises.

11
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:57.957
Because BOLD reads blood, not neurons directly, which neural signal drives it?

12
00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:05.397
In 2001, Nikos Logothetis and colleagues recorded with electrodes inside a scanner

13
00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:08.137
in anaesthetized monkey visual cortex.

14
00:01:09.477 --> 00:01:14.637
At some sites under a long visual stimulus, synaptic currents stayed high while

15
00:01:14.637 --> 00:01:16.037
spiking fell near baseline.

16
00:01:17.837 --> 00:01:19.637
Predict: did BOLD stay high or drop?

17
00:01:25.233 --> 00:01:30.733
BOLD stayed high, like the local field potential, the summed synaptic currents near

18
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:37.273
the electrode. So BOLD seems to reflect input and local processing more than spiking

19
00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:44.693
output. The rule: MRI maps brain structure, while functional MRI reads delayed blood

20
00:01:44.693 --> 00:01:50.473
oxygenation. An active patch shows task involvement, not spikes or necessity.

21
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.807
Three limits shape how we read scans.

22
00:01:55.227 --> 00:01:58.187
First, activation never shows a region is needed.

23
00:01:59.407 --> 00:02:02.647
Testing necessity still requires damage or silencing.

24
00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:09.047
Second, averaging scans across people can blur neighbouring regions into false

25
00:02:09.047 --> 00:02:14.467
overlap. Mapping regions inside each person first avoids that blur.

26
00:02:15.517 --> 00:02:19.677
Third, brain-wide links to behaviour across people are usually tiny.

27
00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:27.157
In 2022, Scott Marek and colleagues found a median association of 0.01.

28
00:02:28.497 --> 00:02:31.877
The median imaging study used about 25 people.

29
00:02:33.057 --> 00:02:36.177
Two such subsamples could support opposite conclusions.

30
00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:40.657
Replication improved only as samples reached thousands.

31
00:02:41.697 --> 00:02:45.597
Fix targets in advance, and test on people kept out of training.

32
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.560
With those guards, scans unlocked discoveries.

33
00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:57.880
In 2007, Nina Dronkers and colleagues scanned Paul Broca's two preserved 1861 brains

34
00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:04.900
with MRI. Both lesions reached deeper, into white matter, than Broca could measure

35
00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:11.780
from the surface. In 2011, Evelina Fedorenko and colleagues defined each person's

36
00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.180
language regions individually.

37
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.480
Most responded little to arithmetic, working memory, or music.

38
00:03:19.633 --> 00:03:25.733
In 2012, Baliki, Apkarian and colleagues followed adults with recent back pain, not

39
00:03:25.733 --> 00:03:27.033
yet chronic, for a year.

40
00:03:28.413 --> 00:03:33.853
Stronger baseline connectivity, correlated activity between medial prefrontal cortex

41
00:03:33.853 --> 00:03:37.013
and nucleus accumbens, predicted persistence.

42
00:03:38.433 --> 00:03:40.953
The ROC area was 0.83.

43
00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:48.013
That means in about 83% % of random pairs, the persisting patient scored higher than

44
00:03:48.013 --> 00:03:49.013
the recovering one.

45
00:03:50.313 --> 00:03:51.533
Prediction is not cause.

46
00:03:52.973 --> 00:03:57.913
Read structure directly, and read every glow as delayed blood oxygenation, not

47
00:03:57.913 --> 00:03:58.253
spikes.
